  "result": "**Scope.** I will not derive PPO here. Training models and the math inside them is out of scope in your mission, and a derivation needs policy gradients and probability, which your files show you have not covered yet.\n\n**Overview of RL for agents**\n- Labs often train tool-calling with RL. The model attempts a task, a reward scores the outcome, and the weights shift toward higher-reward behavior.\n- PPO is one update rule for this. It limits how far each update can move the model from its previous version, which keeps training stable.\n\n**Why it does not fit your project**\n- It needs a model you can modify, thousands of scored runs, and GPU budget. Your sponsor's model budget is small.\n- Reliable tool calling for your assistant is usually reached more cheaply:\n  - Write precise tool descriptions.\n  - Make the booking steps a fixed workflow.\n  - Return clear error messages from tools.\n  - Evaluate on a test set of real student questions.\n\n**Optional route**\n- If you want RL in your mission, tell me and we will update `MISSION.md` together. I would suggest a short separate lesson on it, after your core topics.\n\n**Check:** For a \"book the laser cutter Friday at 3\" request, which steps would you hard-code, and which would you leave to the model?",
